1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:08,200
Same CRF. Slower preset.

2
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:17,690
Better? Measure size and quality.

3
00:00:17,690 --> 00:00:24,750
2 synthetic clips, 10 s each.

4
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:35,330
8 presets, CRF 23, SSIM against a lossless copy.

5
00:00:35,330 --> 00:00:46,810
Test pattern: 0.9936 to 0.9972.

6
00:00:46,810 --> 00:00:58,300
Mandelbrot: about 0.982 to 0.989.

7
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:08,360
ultrafast 2.2 MB, then veryfast 835 kB.

8
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:18,420
Then it rises. Only slower beats veryfast.

9
00:01:18,420 --> 00:01:27,570
slower took 5 to 6 times as long as ultrafast.

10
00:01:27,570 --> 00:01:32,150
Mandelbrot: veryfast smaller than medium.

11
00:01:32,150 --> 00:01:40,250
Held: ultrafast to veryfast, medium to slower.

12
00:01:40,250 --> 00:01:51,830
Not at every step. Two clips are not your footage.

13
00:01:51,830 --> 00:01:58,870
Same CRF holds quality. Presets trade time for size.

14
